# fixedbugs, defect 2501, lane b34-fsl, 2026-11-13.
#
# SYMPTOM: every linker folds the references of a name nothing defines past
# a count, `ld.lld` and `lld-link` past three, GNU ld past five in a row,
# ld64 past seven, so a module whose every reference fell past it was told
# nowhere: this program's three modules each bind `top2501`, a macro for
# `base2501`, and both modules it uses refer to it from eight functions, so
# one module stands past the fold whatever order the link gives them.
#
# CAUSE: the reading placed the references the linker listed, and no other.
#
# FIX: a folded name is asked of each object of the link alone
# (`cli/link_again.hero`), kept by the object's key, and every object needing
# it is read as a reference, so each module is told on every linker.
use fixedbugs2501/a_first
use fixedbugs2501/b_second

extern "fixedbugs-2501-alias.h"
    function top2501() -> i32  #~ ffi_missing_link

function main()
    print(a_first.total() + b_second.total() + top2501())
